<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for Holy Paladin Healer in Wrath of the Lich King Classic for Phase 4. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from Heroics, reputation rewards, and the new 10-man Raid loot added to Titan Rune Dungeons.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot-gear">Holy Paladin Healer Best in Slot Gear, Gems, and Enchants - Pre-Raid Phase 4</h2>The primary thing to aim for in pre-raid is for a few big ticket items that you'll continue to use well into raiding, primarily trinkets which stay very similar for the entire expansion. While your full set will not and does not have to look like this when stepping into your first raid, this set of gear will ensure that you're more than qualified to heal even the hardest encounters in the raid, as well as making you more than powerful enough to heal most raids very handily.<br/>
<br/>You will primarily want to get the trinkets and libram, as all 3 of these will be part of your endgame raiding BiS for the rest of the game. However, the legs and boots are also very good and the legs in particular are extremely close to BiS for the entire phase.<br/>
<br/>Due to Alliance and Horde having differently named items for TOC gear, both faction items have been listed where TOC items are used; however, be aware that stat-wise all of the Alliance/<wbr/>Horde items are identical and there are no gearing changes.<br/>Additionally, since the socket bonuses for this specific gearset are all very poor, we have opted to use a Nightmare Tear instead of an orange and green gem to fulfill the meta gem bonus. As per the gemming guidelines, this is generally a preference-based option and hitting two socket bonuses, even if they're just SP, has slightly higher stat totals.<br/>
<br/>
