<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Shield - <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=60653/enchant-shield-greater-intellect">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Shield - Greater Intellect</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Rings - <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44636/enchant-ring-greater-spellpower">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Ring - Greater Spellpower</span></a> (Enchanting)</div></li></ul>For both the helm and shoulder enchants, you can pick purely off preference. The first enchant listed is more sustain focused, while the latter is more throughput focused. Both are about equally weighted in terms of total stat value; the MP5 is just better for sustain, while the Crit is better for throughput.</div>